# `domain` module

Innermost boundary. Zero framework dependencies.

## Allowed dependencies

None. This is the core — it knows no other module.

## Forbidden in this module

- `org.springframework..`
- `jakarta.persistence..`
- `jakarta.validation..`
- `com.fasterxml.jackson..`
- `tools.jackson..`

The `ArchHook.java check` hook blocks these imports post-edit, based on
`.claude/forbidden-imports.txt`. If you need one of these, the responsibility is in the
wrong module — move the code, not the rule.

